{"step_index":7621,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T17:41:59Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T17:41:59Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T17:42:01Z\nThe search for \"\"roles/storage.objectUser\" permissions site:cloud.google.com\" returned the following summary:\nThe **Storage Object User** role (`roles/storage.objectUser`) in Google Cloud provides permissions to **create, read, update, and delete objects** and multipart uploads within Cloud Storage[1][2].\n\n### Key Details:\n*   **Purpose:** This role is typically used to grant principals the ability to manage objects (files) within a bucket or managed folder without granting them full control over the bucket itself (such as the ability to delete the bucket or change its configuration)[2][3].\n*   **Permissions:** It includes permissions to interact with objects and their metadata[2]. It does **not** include the `storage.buckets.list` permission, meaning users with only this role may not be able to list buckets in the Google Cloud console unless they are granted additional permissions or navigate directly to a known bucket path[4][5].\n*   **Common Use Cases:**\n    *   Allowing service accounts or users to upload/remove objects from a specific managed folder[3].\n    *   Granting read/write access to data for applications or pipelines[4][6].\n\nFor a complete and current list of all individual permissions included in this role, you can consult the [official Google Cloud IAM roles documentation](https://cloud.google.com/iam/docs/understanding-roles) or the Google Cloud console's \"Roles\" page[2][7].\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG2hTut4lC9_CvNqorwu7xgd0KpC3w4BVmL6onM6JgeOa_NJaHTM3NVyeCoiZvL3X7LvToGo9xYPewi1AntzGJAgAsLWWKAlpxV-Lj8ZmH6QuA5R2ozKNeeV8SDv2obQFCsBBMsExeh6ZhfkZK_DKzBKe7ffIg=)\n[2] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGnXynuHh7dxAoHjha7shmGas8aP-pv9SJaP5oL