.  Google Drive's personal accounts have a 15 GB limit, and service accounts cannot upload to My Drive. Shared Drives, however, allow 750 GB daily uploads with 5 TB file size limits.\n\n\nConsidering the data size (3.5 GB to 25 GB) and destination options, Google Cloud Storage's unlimited capacity easily handles the transfer, supporting files up to 5 TB.  While a Google Drive personal account (15 GB) would likely be insufficient, service accounts cannot upload directly to My Drive.\n\n\n"}
